<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cimmerians</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th–7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cimmerians were a nomadic people from the steppe north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> who invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in the eighth and seventh centuries BCE; Assyrian records call them Gimirri. They overran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phrygia">Phrygia</a>, killed the Lydian king Gyges in the mid-seventh century and raided the Greek cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a>, before being driven out by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydians">Lydians</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alyattes">Alyattes</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cimmerians.jpg" alt="Cimmerians" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antiquistik · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cimmerian_Migrations.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
